# 🏁: each 🆕🐟/🆕🦐 call directly invokes 🐠's inherited error-prone initializer, and must release its own raw
# allocation without deinitializing it if the call errors, since 🐠's initializer only releases the receiver itself
# when the receiver's runtime class info is its own, which is never the case when it is inherited like this.
@ ^fn_1f3c1$
+ %alloc = call ptr @ejcAlloc\(
+ call void @ejcReleaseWithoutDeinit\(ptr %alloc\)
+ %alloc15 = call ptr @ejcAlloc\(
+ call void @ejcReleaseWithoutDeinit\(ptr %alloc15\)
+ %alloc32 = call ptr @ejcAlloc\(
+ call void @ejcReleaseWithoutDeinit\(ptr %alloc32\)
+ %alloc49 = call ptr @ejcAlloc\(
+ call void @ejcReleaseWithoutDeinit\(ptr %alloc49\)
